; demand_multi_adorn_allfree_1 -- an ALL-4-MODES-DIAGNOSTIC case under -demand
; (the .drflags sidecar passes the flag; flag-off this program compiles fine and
; is exercised nowhere else). THE ALL-FREE-SIBLING FENCE (D3.a.3 multi-adornment):
; a query NAME carrying a BOUND adornment (q(bound,free)) AND an all-free sibling
; (q(free,free)) shares ONE query materialization with its bound siblings, so the
; all-free cursor would read the demand-GUARDED pub and silently UNDER-answer
; (only the demanded rows). The demand pass REJECTS the whole name (Demand.cpp,
; the per-adornment bound_indices.empty() arm) -- the pre-D3.a.3 per-name belt's
; guarantee, preserved as a clean diagnostic once the per-name reject was lifted
; for the supported bound+bound multi-adornment shape (demand_multi_adorn_witness).
; An all-free-ONLY query name is demand-inert and compiles (it never enters the
; per-adornment loop); this fence fires only on the bound+all-free MIX.
#message edge_2(u64 A, u64 B).
#local rel(u64 A, u64 B).
rel(A, B) : edge_2(A, B).
#query q(bound u64 A, free u64 B).
#query q(free u64 A, free u64 B).
q(A, B) : rel(A, B).
